      ],
      "text": "**Probably yes for an easy jog, if you’re generally healthy.** At about **12:45 a.m. Penang time on October 18**, the latest George Town reading I found was **89 on the US AQI scale (“Moderate”)**, measured at midnight. The nearby Minden station’s last reported Malaysian API reading was **64 (“Moderate”) at 11 p.m.** These are different index scales, but neither reading was in its unhealthy range. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/penang/george-town))\n\nKeep it short and easy rather than doing a hard workout. If you have asthma or a heart or lung condition, consider exercising indoors instead; people unusually sensitive to pollution are advised to limit prolonged or heavy exertion when air quality is moderate. Stop if you develop coughing, wheezing, chest tightness or unusual breathlessness. Air quality can vary across Penang, so check the reading nearest your route before heading out. ([airnow.gov](https://www.airnow.gov/sites/default/files/2018-04/aqi_brochure_02_14_0.pdf?utm_source=openai))",
